The SAML 2.0 service provider (internal/saml, with its test captures) and the
embedded-database layer (internal/sqlitedb) come from Perfuse
(https://github.com/biodream-llc/perfuse), as does the manual renderer
(internal/manual: render.go, page.go, style.go and chapters.go). Perfuse is
Copyright 2026 BioDream LLC and licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0;
its licence and notice are in licenses/perfuse-LICENSE and
licenses/perfuse-NOTICE. These files have been modified for prova. Perfuse
itself stays under the Apache License 2.0; prova's licence does not apply to it.

The OpenID Connect client (internal/oidc) and the account and session design
(internal/auth, internal/authweb) come from Vaglio (BioDream LLC).

The payments casebook (internal/qcasebook/payments.cb) is written in the
casebook language of BioDream's quorum reasoning engine and compiled by quorum's
cbc compiler; the compiled framework is embedded in prova. The optional
prova-proof companion (proof/) is part of prova and under the same licence.

prova-proof may be linked against CaDiCaL (Copyright (c) Armin Biere and
contributors, MIT License), which is obtained and built separately and is not
included in this repository.

The embedded database engine is modernc.org/sqlite (BSD-3-Clause), a
translation of SQLite, which is in the public domain. The Go binary also embeds
goja (MIT) and gopher-lua (MIT). The web interface is built with open-source
packages (React, Redux Toolkit, Vite, Tailwind CSS, CodeMirror, Apache ECharts,
TradingView lightweight-charts, @xyflow/react, @tanstack/react-table, lucide and
others, under the MIT, ISC, BSD and Apache-2.0 licences), listed with their
licences in web/pnpm-lock.yaml.

The ISO 20022 message schemas in internal/validate/xsd are the official schemas
published by ISO 20022 (iso20022.org), taken from the moov-io/iso20022 and
moov-io/fedwire20022 repositories (Apache License 2.0), unchanged.

The card-security test vectors (internal/cardcrypto/testdata) were computed with
psec and pyemv (MIT), the ISO 8583 dialect vectors (internal/iso8583/testdata)
with pyiso8583 (MIT), and the HSM client is tested against the pythales
simulator (LGPL); these are test oracles, run outside prova and not included
in it. The MT940 test reads prova's output with mt-940 (BSD) in the same way.
The test keys in internal/testkeys are published test values, not real keys.

The SEPA rules follow the European Payments Council's public implementation
guidelines; the FedNow rules follow the FedNow Service operating procedures.
prova is not endorsed by the EPC or the Federal Reserve.

